Hook method to handle a single cell.
See {@link Reasoner#apply()} for what it returns when.
However, if a command is returned, it will not have been executed.

@param cell
		the empty cell
@return command to apply, or null if not applicable
@throws NullPointerException
		if {@code cell == null}
@pre {@code cell != null && cell.isEmpty()}
@post {@code (\result == null  ==>  puzzle is not solvable and not modified) &&
(\result.size() > 0  ==>  ! \result.isExecuted() && puzzle.isValid())}

properties.sourceText:
@java.lang.Override
public ypa.command.CompoundCommand apply() {
    final ypa.command.CompoundCommand result = super.apply();
    // repeatedly apply reasoner until no change occurs
    ypa.command.CompoundCommand compound;
    do {
        compound = this.reasoner.apply();
        if (compound == null) {
            result.revert();// HARD-TO-FIND DEFECT IF OMITTED!

            return compound;
        }
        result.addAll(compound);
    } while (compound.size() > 0 );
    // 
    return result;
}

